 "version": 1,
 "about": "Inputs of the agents16 simulation. Run timelines are the recorded gate runs of 10-27 (gate-g-tools/run/g4x-*.json for wall and peak RSS, the live footprint store estimates-1450.json for the footprint peak and its time): fp = tree footprint in MB at the end of the segment (macOS phys_footprint, what the governor observes and learns), rss = product.py tree RSS in MB (reference only; 2.5-3x the footprint). A segment's footprint ramps linearly from the previous level to fp over peakAt seconds (default: the whole segment) and then holds. Segment kinds: door (process chain start), served (graph from the memo), plan (graph planned by a child), refresh (graph rebuilt: needs the single builder custody; a cold builder asks the project farm for workers after farmAfter seconds), bazel (needs a Bazel session slot; the slot server is part of fp and stays as idle foreign memory afterwards). cpu = cores the segment keeps busy.",
